//RS }
//RS 
//RS // #2003 — this definition is DELIBERATELY separate from the compiler's
//RS // in-process copy, and it is the only legitimate second one.
//RS //
//RS // This fragment is embedded verbatim into every generated program. A generated
//RS // program is a standalone Rust crate that links no Jet crate, so it cannot call
//RS // `jet-jit`'s `CoreHost::jit_env_value_raw`, and the fragment cannot be
//RS // `include!`d into `jet-jit` either: it reaches its table through
//RS // `jet_env_read()`, which the generated crate defines and the host does not.
//RS // The host side therefore carries exactly ONE mirror of this lookup —
//RS // `CoreHost::jit_env_value_raw` — which the resident JIT, the extern "C" heap
//RS // shims and the interpreter ambient all call. Two definitions total, one per
//RS // linkage world; adding a third in any engine is an I9 violation.
//RS //
//RS // Raw `OsString` on purpose: `NO_COLOR` counts by PRESENCE, so a value that is
